<h2>The statutory pieces, assembled</h2>
<table class="law">
  <tr><th>Provision</th><th>What it mandates</th></tr>
  <tr><td>Section 173(1) BNSS</td><td>Information of a cognizable offence shall be received irrespective of the area of commission (Zero FIR), orally, in writing or by electronic communication; electronic information is taken on record on signature within three days</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Section 173(1) safeguards</td><td>For specified sexual offences against women, recording by a woman officer; for disabled victims, recording at residence or place of choice with interpreter or special educator and videography</td></tr>
